description:
Feature: Papyrus can integrate from the Prospectus docs alone
  Scenario: A Papyrus engineer reads docs/accounts/PAPYRUS_SITES.md
    Then it gives the exact request, response and error contract for:
      - CLI enrollment through cli-login's prepare and enroll hooks: a challenge bound to sha256hex(T), resolve with loginState T;
      - account selection (X-Prospectus-Account is a choice that the site checks with POST /v1/accounts/{id}/authorize);
      - whoami through GET /v1/identities/me;
      - account creation, membership changes, and the lifecycle events;
    And it says which call fails closed and how reenrollment_required reaches the CLI

Source: the answers sent to the Papyrus session on 2026-10-31.
